<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Finding the mistake in a phase shift</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Baraka says: <q>The graph of \(y = \sin({@b@}x + {@cc@}^\circ)\) is the graph of \(y = \sin {@b@}x\) translated \({@cc@}^\circ\) to the left.</q></p><p>(a) Which statement is correct?</p><div>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Find the \(x\)-coordinate of the first maximum point of \(y = \sin({@b@}x + {@cc@}^\circ)\) with \(x \gt 0\).</p><div>[[input:ans2]] \(^\circ\) [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) \({@b@}x + {@cc@}^\circ = {@b@}(x + {@sh@}^\circ)\), so \(y = \sin({@b@}x + {@cc@}^\circ)\) is \(y = \sin {@b@}x\) with \(x\) replaced by \(x + {@sh@}^\circ\): a translation of \({@sh@}^\circ\) to the left, not \({@cc@}^\circ\). The graph moves the opposite way to the sign, by the angle divided by \({@b@}\). So the correct statement is the one that gives a shift of \({@sh@}^\circ\) to the left.</p><p>(b) Sine is greatest when its angle is \(90^\circ\): \({@b@}x + {@cc@} = 90\), so \(x = \dfrac{90 - {@cc@}}{{@b@}} = {@mx@}^\circ\). Check: the maximum of \(y = \sin {@b@}x\) is at \({@m3@}^\circ\), and \({@m3@}^\circ - {@sh@}^\circ = {@mx@}^\circ\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* Design: find the mistake in a phase shift. Options are fixed letters; only their display text carries the seed's numbers. The display order is permuted by entry: the correct option C is shown second, third or fourth (perm), never first. Source: original. */
L: [[2,60],[3,15],[2,40],[3,75],[5,40],[6,30],[2,80],[3,30],[5,15],[6,60]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
b: L[ix][1]; cc: L[ix][2];
sh: cc/b; mx: (90-cc)/b;
m1: 90-cc; m2: 90/b-cc; m3: 90/b;
opts0: [["A",false,sconcat("Baraka is right: adding ", string(cc), "\\(^\\circ\\) inside the bracket moves the graph ", string(cc), "\\(^\\circ\\) to the left.")],
 ["B",false,"Baraka is wrong: the plus sign means the graph moves to the right."],
 ["C",true,sconcat("Baraka is wrong: \\(\\sin(", string(b), "x + ", string(cc), "^\\circ) = \\sin ", string(b), "(x + ", string(sh), "^\\circ)\\), so the graph moves ", string(sh), "\\(^\\circ\\) to the left.")],
 ["D",false,"Baraka is wrong: adding an angle inside the bracket changes the period of the wave."]];

perm: [[1,3,2,4],[2,4,3,1],[4,1,2,3],[4,3,1,2],[2,1,3,4],[1,4,2,3],[2,3,4,1],[4,2,3,1],[1,2,4,3],[4,1,3,2]];
opts: makelist(opts0[perm[ix][j]], j, 1, 4);
mx7: mx+7;
nice(v) := block([r], r: floor(1000*v+1/2)/1000, if integerp(r) then r else float(r));
mxlate: mx + 360/b;
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
